*NISM VIII - T2.1 - about 32 min read*

## Learning objectives
- Calculate portfolio Delta and Gamma sensitivities
- Deploy Covered Call and Protective Put strategies

## What is it?
Option Greeks measure option price sensitivities. Delta measures rate of change per rupee move in spot stock. Theta measures daily time decay. Vega measures price change per 1% change in implied volatility.

## Why it matters
Professional traders manage risk by hedging Greeks rather than predicting directional market moves.

## How it works
Call Delta ranges from 0 to +1 (ATM ≈ +0.5). Put Delta ranges from 0 to -1 (ATM ≈ -0.5). Covered Call involves holding long stock and writing an OTM Call option.

## Key definitions
- **Delta (Δ)** - Change in option price per 1-unit change in underlying spot price.
- **Theta (θ)** - Daily time decay of option premium (erodes buyer value).
- **Vega (ν)** - Sensitivity of option price to changes in Implied Volatility.

## Rules & regulations
- Short option positions require upfront SPAN and Extreme Loss Margins maintained at all times.
- Brokers must issue real-time margin alerts when losses breach 70% of initial margin deposit.

## Formulas
- **Option Premium Decomposition:** `Option Premium = Intrinsic Value + Time Value`
  - *Example:* Spot stock = ₹1,550. Strike 1,500 Call trades at ₹75 premium. Intrinsic Value = 1550 - 1500 = ₹50. Time Value = 75 - 50 = ₹25.

## Practical scenario
An investor holding 500 shares of Reliance at ₹3,000 fears a short-term drop after quarterly earnings. They buy a 2,900 Put option for ₹40. If Reliance crashes to ₹2,600, the put option gains ₹260 in intrinsic value, protecting the portfolio.

## Common mistakes
- Thinking an OTM option has negative intrinsic value; intrinsic value can never be less than zero.

## Quick revision slides
**1. Option Greeks at a Glance**
- Delta: Price sensitivity (Call: 0 to +1, Put: -1 to 0)
- Theta: Time decay (accelerates rapidly in the final 10 days to expiry)
- Vega: Volatility sensitivity (highest for ATM options)',32,1,3) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET course_id=excluded.course_id,module_id=excluded.module_id,title=excluded.title,kind=excluded.kind,body=excluded.body,minutes=excluded.minutes,published=excluded.published,sort=excluded.sort;
